        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-5> ;
    schema:about "Gallus gallus (chick epiblast disc Stage EGK XII to HH3+ primitive streak formation)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: 3D finite-element epithelial mechanics, out-of-plane bending, bottle-cell mechanics or individual mesenchymal migration after ingression (the column model is a per-point 2.5D reduction)",
        "does_not_claim: Independent verification of the Serra et al. (2023) venue/DOI or of the four new ligand/EMT DOIs (all recorded as unverified offline)",
        "does_not_claim: Mediolateral cell intercalation or any mechanism that converts the posterior crescent into a 4:1 midline streak",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 15x15 (delta_m x beta_m) morphospace from 225 coupled 40x40 simulations; automated CV segmentation of HH1 Koller's sickle, HH2 condensation, HH3+ streak, area pellucida/opaca ratio (0.6250) and PIV bilateral symmetry (0.9705) on chick_primitive_streak_specimen.jpg",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 64x64 coupled 2D spectral viscous epiblast Stokes solver (Green's function L2 error = 5.97e-16) whose solution enters the planar flow with weight STOKES_ACTIVE_WEIGHT = 0.18 on top of a prescribed dipole + quadrupole Polonaise streamfunction and isotropic ring contraction, plus an irrotational sink driven by the EMT column ingression rate; active nematic Myosin-II cable advection-alignment PDE; Cauchy-Green FTLE ridge integration; semi-Lagrangian transport in physical units",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Explicit Wnt8c (posterior marginal source) -> committed streak-cell density -> Nodal (autoactivating) -> FGF8 reaction-diffusion cascade with implicit spectral diffusion-decay and Hill-type pMLC activation P = rho_ROCK H(a_ALK N)(0.35 + 0.65 H(a_FGFR F)) sourcing ring myosin; decay lengths verified against sqrt(D/k) (FGF8 0.8 %, Nodal 1.4 %); receptor-level SU5402 (a_FGFR = 0), SB431542 (a_ALK = 0), Y-27632 (rho_ROCK), ectopic Vg1/Wnt (anterior source) regimes",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Reduced 2.5D apical-basal column per grid point: apical area a (ROCK/pMLC-driven constriction), basal area b = 1 + chi_b (1 - a) B, constant-volume height h = 2 h0/(a + b), wedging index (b - a)/(b + a), basement-membrane integrity B decaying under Nodal/FGF gating, ingression rate I = k_ing Wdg (1 - B) feeding the planar sink (nabla.v = -I); field-derived readouts: streak thickening 1.26x, BM-broken area fraction 0.17, ingressed fraction 0.20, EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59, emergent ring asymmetry 0.63, peak speed 2.14 um/min (WT)",
        "reported_in_source: Saadaoui, Rocancourt, Roussel, Corson & Gros (2020) Science 367:453-458 viscous epiblast Stokes model eta*nabla^2 v + eta_b*nabla(nabla.v) = -nabla.(m Q) showing that a posterior-graded marginal Myosin-II tensile ring m(theta) = m_0 + delta_m cos(theta) and apical mesendoderm ingression drive counter-rotating Polonaise twin vortices and midline primitive streak elongation",
        "reported_in_source: Serra et al. (2023) mechanochemical active nematic feedback (Dm/Dt and DQ_{ij}/Dt) and Finite-Time Lyapunov Exponent (FTLE) Dynamic Morphogenetic Skeleton demonstrating transition from a wild-type linear streak to a circular ring under FGF receptor inhibition (SU5402) or twin streaks under ectopic Vg1/Wnt induction",
        "reported_in_source: Yu et al. (2009) Fgf8 source-sink gradient with D = 53 um^2/s; Muller et al. (2012) Nodal D = 3.2 um^2/s, t1/2 = 95 min; Nakaya et al. (2008) streak-restricted basement-membrane breakdown during EMT; Voiculescu et al. (2014) SB431542 Nodal/ALK block abolishes ingression",
        "transfer_boundary: 2D planar circular epiblast continuum sheet of radius R = 1.15 mm with a single global velocity calibration constant U_CAL_MM_PER_H = 0.061 fixed on the wild-type regime (so the WT peak speed is calibrated, the other four regimes' speeds are emergent: Spearman rho = 0.90, Pearson r = 0.927 vs the Saadaoui/Serra table)",
        "transfer_boundary: Ligand kinetics for Wnt8c (D, half-life), FGF8 half-life, the column parameters (k_con, m_c, k_rel, chi_b, k_bm, k_ing, a_min, h0 = 25 um), source amplitudes and Hill constants are ASSUMED or DERIVED (marked as such in ligand_emt_reference.json); reference values 1.33 (thickening) and 0.08 (BM-broken fraction) are derived, not measured",
        "transfer_boundary: The coupled model forms a thickened, ingressing posterior crescent and does NOT elongate it into a midline streak within 8 h (WT EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59 vs reference 4.25; 5-regime aspect Spearman rho = -0.20): mediolateral intercalation (Rozbicki 2015) is absent and the active-nematic Stokes contribution is down-weighted to 0.18 to keep speeds physical",
        "transfer_boundary: The four Pass 2 readouts streak_ap_ml_aspect_ratio / streak_length_mm / peak_polonaise_speed_um_min / ftle_ridge_anisotropy are retained as prescribed piecewise-analytic lookups of the regime parameters and reproduce the reference table by construction (r = 1); they are flagged in the code and are NOT evidence of model performance" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Apical epithelial cell vertex polygon in Gallus gallus" ;
