<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — Code-to-model traceability: 74/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: each new modelling function carries a docstring stating its equation and biological reading (ligand cascade, pMLC activation, column wedging, sink), the circular lookups and circular correlations are flagged with NOTE comments at the point of computation, the math KG YAML registers the two new laws with Lean declarations and current code loci and carries an audit_note on law 3, and 5 Lean theorems compile with 0 sorrys. Deductions: run_self_test's docstring still says 'Pass 2 verification suite ... all 3 Lean 4 theorem invariants' while the suite tests five (-4); the retained Pass 2 measurement names ('wild-type HH3 primitive streak AP/ML aspect ratio', '5-regime ... Pearson correlation r') describe lookups as if they were model outputs (-6); the segmentation docstring's 0.6406 contradicts the code (-3); OUTPUT_LIGAND_PNG is declared but never rendered (-2); the module header still cites the unverified Serra venue/DOI and the Lean theorem 1 (circulation conservation) is traced to a prescribed psi rather than to a solved field, which the YAML audit_note only partly says (-3); Pass 2's Lean theorem 3 constants aspect100_*/v100_* are the reference table itself (-4, flagged in the YAML)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py L105–L107: OUTPUT_LIGAND_PNG declared but never rendered (dead constant) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py#L105-L107>",
        "2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py L1727–L1731: run_self_test docstring stale: 'Pass 2 verification suite ... all 3 Lean 4 theorem invariants' (5 theorems exist) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py#L1727-L1731>",
        "morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_050_gastrulation_streak_attractor.lean L165–L198: Theorem 3's aspect100_*/v100_* constants are the reference table itself <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_050_gastrulation_streak_attractor.lean#L165-L198>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — Model fidelity to source: 68/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the spectral Stokes operator eta lap v + eta_b grad(div v) = -div(m Q) is correct (Green's function error 5.97e-16); the active nematic Dm/Dt, DQ/Dt equations with strain-rate alignment and corotation are implemented; transport is now unconditionally stable semi-Lagrangian in mm/h (+); the new Wnt8c/Nodal/FGF8 cascade uses implicit spectral diffusion-decay with sourced diffusivities and verified decay lengths (+); the column model gives a constant-volume wedging/thickening law with ROCK-, Nodal- and FGF-gated BM breakdown whose ingression rate closes the loop into the planar divergence (+); the ligand->pMLC->ring asymmetry chain and the wedging->sink chain are each backed by a Lean theorem. Deductions: the planar flow is dominated by a prescribed dipole + quadrupole streamfunction and an isotropic ring-contraction term, with the Stokes solution entering at weight 0.18 (-12) — the Green's-function test validates the solver, not the model flow, and Theorem 1's circulation conservation is a symmetry of the prescribed psi; the coupled model does not form a streak (WT EMT-zone AP/ML 0.59 vs 4.25) because mediolateral intercalation is absent and the nematic feedback is too weak to elongate the crescent at physical speeds (-10); the four prescribed lookup readouts are still computed and exported alongside the honest ones (-4); ALPHA_M_HR is set to 0.10 against the vendored 0.45 without changing the JSON (-3); the column model is a per-point 2.5D reduction, not the requested 3D coupling, and the ligand fields are clipped by soft_wall each substep as a crude absorbing boundary while Wnt8c's 72 um decay length is below the 40 um grid's resolving power (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py L114–L125: U_CAL_MM_PER_H fixed on WT; ALPHA_M_HR = 0.10 deviates from the vendored 0.45; STOKES_ACTIVE_WEIGHT, GAMMA_Q_HR, D_M, D_Q unsourced <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py#L114-L125>",
        "2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py L649–L667: Prescribed psi_dip / psi_quad streamfunction and iso_ring_v* dominate the planar velocity; Stokes solution enters with STOKES_ACTIVE_WEIGHT = 0.18; EMT sink added in physical units <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py#L649-L667>",
        "2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py L812–L843: Retained piecewise-analytic lookup for streak_ap_ml / streak_len / peak_speed / ftle_aniso — reproduces the reference table by construction (flagged in NOTE) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/028758bc/2022-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor.py#L812-L843>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-7>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-model-fidelity-8> ;
    pk1:hasScore 6.8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-serra-gastrulation-streak-attractor-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Saadaoui et al. (2020), Serra et al. (2023) & Rozbicki et al. (2015) avian gastrulation tensile ring, Polonaise twin-vortex flow & primitive streak attractor — Morphometric validation: 62/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: measure_morphoeval() now returns 14 measurements, of which the 7 new Pass 3 ones are field-derived and honest — FGF8 decay length 373.9 vs 371.0 um analytic, WT emergent ring asymmetry 0.63 vs 0.74 HH1 initial, 5-regime emergent speed Spearman rho 0.90, 5-regime EMT-zone aspect Spearman rho -0.20 (reported as a failure), WT thickening 1.26 vs 1.33, SB431542 ingressed fraction 0.0 vs 0.0, WT BM-broken area fraction 0.17 vs 0.08 — and the figure's Panel I prints them (+). Deductions: four of the seven retained Pass 2 measurements ('wild-type HH3 primitive streak AP/ML 4.25', 'peak speed 2.40', '5-regime r = 1.0000', 'SU5402 AP/ML 1.00') are lookups that reproduce their own reference values and are still emitted as if they were model outputs (-14); the thickening (1.33) and BM-fraction (0.08) reference values are DERIVED in the JSON, not measured chick values, and the BM-fraction measurement misses its target by 2x (-6); the PIV symmetry reference 0.9705 is the script's own output and the 5.00x specimen fold change is partly hard-coded in the figure (-6); the WT peak speed (2.14 um/min) is calibrated by construction via U_CAL_MM_PER_H and so is not an independent validation (-4); only n = 5 regimes enter the rank correlations, so rho = 0.90 carries little statistical weight (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
